(if: $naomiAlone)[(set: $naomiFound to true, $naomi to it - 20)(display: "clamp")Naomi isn't at the library. Her table is empty.

You find her in the back stairwell, the one nobody uses, sitting on the steps with her hood up.

"I worked it out last night," she says, without turning around. "After you didn't come. Two weeks ago I told someone Iris was freaking out about money. That's all I said. I didn't say Hale." She pulls her sleeves over her hands. "But I said her name. And now she can't even go to the dining hall."

"It's not my fault people are idiots." Quieter: "It's not my fault people are idiots."

She doesn't believe it either time.](else:)[Naomi is in the back stairwell, the one nobody uses. She texted you to come. She hasn't slept.

"I keep reading what people say about her," she says. "And all I can think is, it started with my sentence."]

(if: $switches > 0)[(link: "▸ see what she's thinking")[(set: $switches to it - 1, $hauntNaomi to true)<span class="thought naomi">It's loud in here. Every thought is pointed at herself. //Stupid. You knew it was private. You said it anyway because you wanted to sound like you knew things.// //I'm the reason. I'm always the reason.// //don't let him see.//</span>]]

