:: Day 6 [bg-room-mc night hub]
(save-game: "auto")(set: $lockI to $iris < 15, $lockN to $naomi < 15, $capI to $iris < 40, $capN to $naomi < 40, $frzI to $iris, $frzN to $naomi)<div class="dayhead">SATURDAY</div><div class="whisper">...</div>
You can't sleep, so you scroll.

You open your messages with Naomi. You just want something from before. Some dumb meme. Proof there was a time when everything was normal.

You scroll up. Past this week. Past last week.

And then you stop.

<span class="phone me">iris lost her scholarship lol</span>
<span class="phone me">shes freaking out about money. dont tell anyone</span>
<span class="phone">omg poor thing</span>
<span class="phone">my lips are sealed. obviously</span>

Two weeks ago. 11:48 p.m. You don't even remember sending it.

//Lol.//

Naomi didn't start this. She didn't find it out. She didn't overhear it.

**You told her.**

[[Go outside. Your room is too small.->D6 Bench]]


:: D6 Bench [bg-bench night maeve]
Maeve is sitting on the green bench, swinging her legs, like she's been waiting.

(if: $loop is 2)["Oh, babe," she says softly. "There it is. Again."

"You knew. Both times."

"I know lots of things." She pulls you down next to her and leans into you, cold all the way through. "You took it better this time. Last time you looked at me like I was the way out." She laughs, very quietly. "I'm not, babe. Not for you. Not yet."](else:)["Oh, babe," she says softly. "There it is."

"You knew."

"I know lots of things." She pats the bench. "You look like you want to disappear. That's an option. It always is." Then she tilts her head. "But it's not the interesting one."]

She gets up and walks into the dark between two buildings, and the motion light doesn't come on for her.

(if: $switches > 0)[(link: "▸ see what she's thinking")[(set: $switches to it - 1, $hauntMaeve to true)<span class="thought maeve">Nothing about the rumour. Nothing about Iris, or Naomi, or anyone. Only you, very bright, like the last window lit in a building. //He could still surprise me.// //soon, babe.//</span>]]

[[Morning->D6 Morning]]


:: D6 Morning [bg-room-naomi day naomi]
Naomi opens the door because you've been knocking for three minutes.

"What," she says. Her eyes are red. She hasn't slept either.

Your phone is in your hand. The message is still on the screen.

(link-reveal-goto: "Show her the message.", "D6 Confess")[(set: $confessedNaomi to true, $naomi to it + 15, $baseN to it + 15)(display: "clamp")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Delete it. She never has to know.", "D6 Hide")[(set: $hidNaomi to true)]


:: D6 Confess [bg-room-naomi day naomi]
She reads it. She reads the date. You watch her get it.

"You only knew because I told you," you say. "It didn't start with you. It started with me. I said //lol//, and I forgot I even did it. You've been carrying my thing."

For a second she looks like she's going to slam the door.

"You //forgot//?" She shoves your shoulder. It doesn't hurt. "I've been thinking I was the worst person in the whole... and you //forgot//?"

"I'm sorry."

"Shut up." She pulls you inside by your sleeve. You sit on her bed. Neither of you says anything for a while.

"So we're both idiots," she says finally.

"Yeah."

"Great. Perfect." She leans her head on your shoulder, very briefly, like it's an accident. "That's... actually kind of better. Is that bad?"

"No."

"Don't tell anyone I said that."

[[Later->D6 Afternoon]]


:: D6 Hide [bg-room-naomi day naomi]
You put the phone in your pocket.

"Nothing," you say. "I just wanted to see you."

She looks at you like she doesn't believe a word of it. Then she lets you in anyway. She sits on her bed with her knees up and stares at the wall and says, "It's not my fault people are idiots," twice.

You know exactly whose fault it is. You don't say it.

[[Later->D6 Afternoon]]


