(link-reveal-goto: "Not tonight. She has enough.", "D7 Ask")[(set: $hidIris to true)]


:: D7 Truth [bg-room-iris-clean night iris]
"The rumour. The money part. Naomi told one person, and it grew from there. But Naomi only knew because I told her. Two weeks ago, the night you first told me about the scholarship. I texted her like it was nothing, and I forgot I even did it. I'm so sorry."

Iris doesn't yell. She just closes her eyes.

"Why are you telling me?" she says. "You could've just... never."

"Because things always come out. And I didn't want you to find out alone."

She's quiet for a long time.

[[...->D7 Ask]]


:: D7 Ask [bg-room-iris-clean night iris]
"I'm really tired," Iris says, very small.

And you hear it. Not in the words. In the clean room, and the jacket, and the sketchbook with the hair tie around it.

(link-reveal-goto: "Ask her directly if she's thinking about killing herself.", "D7 Asked")[(set: $askedDirect to true, $iris to it + 15, $baseI to it + 15)(display: "clamp")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Tell her to get some sleep. Things will look better tomorrow.", "D7 Naomi")[(set: $iris to it - 5)(display: "clamp")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Change the subject. Put a movie on.", "D7 Naomi")[(set: $iris to it - 10)(display: "clamp")]


:: D7 Asked [bg-room-iris-clean night iris]
It's the hardest sentence of your life, and it comes out shaking.

"Iris. Are you thinking about killing yourself?"

She looks at you like you've seen straight through a wall she thought was solid.

"...Sometimes," she says. "Tonight. Kind of. Yeah."

"Okay. Thank you for telling me. I'm not going anywhere tonight. Not one minute. And I want us to call someone together. Right now."

She nods. She's crying now, finally, the way she didn't cry on Monday.

You call 988 together on speaker, sitting on her floor. The woman who answers has a calm voice and asks Iris questions, and Iris answers them, slowly at first. You hold her hand the whole time. At the end Iris agrees to go to the counselling centre in the morning, and to call her mom, and to let you come with her.

[[...->D7 Naomi]]


:: D7 Naomi [bg-room-iris-clean night iris]
Your phone is in your hand. Naomi's name is right there.

(link-reveal-goto: "Text Naomi: can you come to iris's. please.", "D7 Door")[(if: $confessedNaomi)[(set: $iris to it + 10, $naomi to it + 10)](else-if: $hidNaomi)[](else:)[(set: $iris to it + 5, $naomi to it + 5)](display: "clamp")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Don't. It's just you and Iris tonight.", "D7 Night")[]


:: D7 Door [bg-room-iris-clean night iris naomi]
(if: $hidNaomi)[You wait an hour. The message says //read//. Nobody knocks.](else:)[(set: $naomiCame to true)Around ten, there's a knock. Naomi is standing in the doorway holding three coffees, looking more scared than you've ever seen her.

"They messed up my order," she says to Iris. "I got too many."

Iris almost laughs.

Naomi sits down on the floor, stiffly, like she's never sat on a floor before. "I'm the one who passed it on," she says. "I'm sorry. I didn't say the Hale thing. But I said your name. And I shouldn't have."

Iris looks at Naomi. Then at you. Two people who passed on her secret, sitting on her floor, holding the coffees they brought her.

"You're both idiots," Iris says. And then, so quietly you barely hear it: "You both came, though."]

[[...->D7 Night]]


:: D7 Night [bg-black night]
Your phone lights up on the carpet.

2:07.

(if: $hidIris)[(set: $iris to it - 15, $leaks to it + 1)(display: "clamp")Iris's phone buzzes at the same moment. She reads it. Then she looks at you for a very long time.

"Some girl just texted me," she says. "White hair. I don't even know how she has my number. She said, //ask him who he told.//"]

[[2:08->Final]]


