(if: (passage:)'s tags contains "iris")[(if: $iris < 35)[<span class="lost">(if: $day < 3)[dont be a lot. dont be a lot.](else-if: $day < 6)[one less thing](else:)[its almost done]</span>](else-if: $iris >= 60)[<span class="glow iris">(if: $day < 4)[maybe tomorrow is okay](else:)[next week. a next-week thing]</span>]]
(if: (passage:)'s tags contains "naomi")[(if: $naomi < 35)[<span class="lost">(if: $naomiFound)[my fault my fault my fault](else:)[who even started this]</span>](else-if: $naomi >= 60 and ($confessedNaomi or $day is 1))[<span class="glow naomi">(if: $confessedNaomi)[we're both idiots. fine.](else:)[he's annoying. stay annoying]</span>](else-if: $day >= 2 and $signDay < $day)[(set: $signDay to $day)<span class="sign">(if: $day is 2)[Her phone buzzes. She doesn't look at it. She always looks at it.](else-if: $day is 3)[Her nails are bitten short. On Monday they were painted.](else-if: $day is 4)[She laughs at something a second late, like she had to remember how.](else-if: $day is 5)[Her hands won't stay still. There's a coffee in front of her she hasn't touched.](else-if: $day is 6)[She looks like she's been awake since Thursday.](else:)[She checks her phone every minute. Iris. It's always Iris.]</span>]]


:: go alone
(set: $alone to it + 1, $aloneToday to it + 1, $iris to it - 2, $naomi to it - 2)(display: "clamp")


:: Alone [bg-hall-white day maeve]
(if: $loop is 1 and not $metMaeve)[(set: $metMaeve to true)You find a bench nobody's using. A minute later, somebody is.

A girl with long white hair and an oversized coat that looks expensive sits down at the other end, like it's her bench and you're the one visiting.

"I'm Maeve," she says, without being asked. "You look like you're having a week, babe."

She doesn't explain the //babe//. She doesn't explain anything. She just watches you, like you're the most interesting thing on campus.](else-if: $aloneToday > 2)[Maeve again. She doesn't say anything this time. She just hums something you almost know, and her shoulder is cold against yours.](else-if: $loop is 2 and $aloneToday > 1)["Twice in one day," Maeve purrs, hooking her arm through yours. "You're going to make me think you like me."

The motion light above her stays off. You're almost sure now.](else-if: $loop is 2)[(if: $day is 1)[Maeve is on the bench by the fountain, exactly where you knew she'd be.

"Oh, you //remember// me," she says, delighted, and pulls you down beside her by your sleeve. "Don't stare, babe. It's rude to stare at a lady who brought you back."

She says it like a joke. Her hands are as cold as last time. Colder. //Seventy-five percent,// you think. Maybe more.](else-if: $day is 2)["Missed me?" Maeve hooks one finger through your belt loop. "You died very nicely last time, you know. Very romantic. Don't do it again."

She winks. You can't tell if she's joking. You're fairly sure she isn't.](else-if: $day is 3)["It's our date night," Maeve sings, walking backwards in front of you. "Or it was. You remember how it ended."

She leans in until her cold nose touches your cheek. "I wouldn't mind a repeat, babe. I'd mind it for them."](else-if: $day is 4)[Maeve is lying across three chairs in the white hallway like she owns them. She doesn't open her eyes.

"You know what I am," she says. "Mostly." One pale eye opens. "Smart boy. Don't say it out loud. It ruins the mood."](else-if: $day is 5)["Babe," Maeve says softly, fixing your collar, "I already had one of you. I don't need the whole set."

She nods toward the stairwell, where Naomi sat this morning. "Go on. Shoo."](else-if: $day is 6)["You didn't get this far last time," Maeve says, and kisses your cheek. It feels like snow. "I'm proud of you. Don't tell anyone. It's bad for business."](else:)["Tonight I'll be around," Maeve says. "Like last time. Like the time before that."

She smooths your hair down with a cold hand. "Make me wait, babe. Make me wait a really, really long time."]](else-if: $aloneToday > 1)[(if: $day is 1)[She's there again, reading a vending machine receipt like it's a novel. "Two in one day. People will talk, babe."](else-if: $day is 2)["Again?" Maeve pats the spot next to her. "I'm not complaining. I like company that doesn't need anything from me."](else-if: $day is 3)[Maeve hands you half a sandwich she definitely didn't buy. "Eat. You look like a ghost." She laughs at something you don't get.](else-if: $day is 4)["Hiding with me again, babe?" She tucks your hair behind your ear. "I don't mind. But they might."](else-if: $day is 5)[She doesn't say anything this time. She just sits close enough that you can feel how cold she is.](else-if: $day is 6)["One more day," she says. "Spend it well, babe. I mean that. I really, really mean that."](else:)[She's gone before you sit down. On the step where she was, there's a coffee, still hot. It isn't yours.]](else:)[(if: $day is 1)[Maeve finds you on the bench by the fountain.

"Monday," she says, like it's a flavour she doesn't like. "Everyone's so loud about that girl." She looks at you sideways. "You're not. Interesting."](else-if: $day is 2)[Maeve is sitting on the radiator in the white hallway, swinging her legs.

"You keep walking away from people," she says. "Is that a hobby?"](else-if: $day is 3)["They're having a hard week," Maeve says, falling into step beside you. "Your two."

She says //your two// like it's obvious. "I'd hate to meet them." Before you can ask what that means, she's asking if you like her coat.](else-if: $day is 4)[Maeve is on the stairs, tracing the handrail with one cold finger.

"Do you know what's funny about weeks?" she says. "They end."](else-if: $day is 5)["Friday," says Maeve. "Everyone's tired on Fridays. Some people more than others."

She looks toward the stairwell, then back at you, and smiles like she's sorry about something.](else-if: $day is 6)["You know now," Maeve says. Not a question. "The text." She makes a face. "Don't do the thing where you disappear, babe. It's so boring. I've seen it a thousand times."](else:)[Maeve is on the steps where Iris usually sits.

"Big night," she says. "I'll be around. I'm always around." She stands and brushes off her coat. "I'd rather not be needed, if it's all the same to you."]]

(link-goto: "Keep going", $next)


:: Revival [bg-black]
Nothing. And then, in the nothing, a voice.

You can't see anyone. There's nobody to see.

<span class="death">Oh. There you are.</span>
<span class="death">Don't panic. You're not anywhere. Not yet.</span>

<span class="death">I watched your week. It ended badly. Hers first, then yours. I don't usually get two from the same little story so close together.</span>

<span class="death">So. A game.</span>

<span class="death">You go back. The same seven days. The rumour has already done its damage, and I can't take that back. Rules are rules.</span>
<span class="death">Every day you choose where to be. You can't be everywhere. Nobody can.</span>
<span class="death">Every night you'll see how they're holding up. Two lines. Watch them.</span>
<span class="death">Five times, I'll let you hear what someone is thinking. Spend them carefully.</span>
<span class="death">And when you walk alone... well. You won't be alone. Someone always turns up.</span>

A pause. It sounds almost fond.

<span class="death">I'd rather not see any of you this week. Any of the three. Make it a quiet week for me, hm?</span>

<span class="death">Go on. Wake up.</span>

[[Wake up->Wake]]


:: Again [bg-black]
Nothing. Then the voice, in the nothing. You know it. You heard it once before, when all of this started.

<span class="death">Oh. That was quick.</span>
<span class="death">You didn't even try for them.</span>

<span class="death">I'll be honest, that doesn't happen. People run away from me. All week, every week, forever.</span>
<span class="death">You ran //to// me.</span>

A sound like someone smiling in the dark.

<span class="death">I'm interested now. That's your fault.</span>
<span class="death">One more time. Keep this week. Remember all of it.</span>
<span class="death">And this time, babe, maybe look at someone other than me.</span>
<span class="death">I've made it a little easier for you. Don't tell anyone.</span>

(set: $loop to 2)(display: "reset vars")
[[Wake up->Wake]]


:: D1 Afternoon [bg-hall-posters day hub]
Afternoon. Your two o'clock gets out early. In the hallway, someone has stuck a note on a poster: a crude drawing and a big letter H. People stop to take pictures of it.

(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devI >= $devN, "Text Iris before she walks down this hallway.", "Iris will see this. Maybe you should go."), "D1 Afternoon Iris")[(display: "pick iris")]
(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devN >= $devI, "Naomi's at the fountain. Go sit with her.", "Naomi's at the fountain. She hasn't texted since lunch."), "D1 Afternoon Naomi")[(display: "pick naomi")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Peel the note off. Walk somewhere quiet by yourself.", "Alone")[(set: $next to "D1 Late")(display: "go alone")]


:: D1 Afternoon Iris [bg-hall-posters day iris]
She's already seen it. She's standing in front of the poster with her bag strap in both fists, very still, like if she moves it'll notice her.

"It's fine," she says. "It's a drawing. It's not even a good drawing."

(link-reveal-goto: "Rip it down. Put it in your pocket.", "D1 Afternoon Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it + 5, $r to "rip")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Take a photo of it. Proof, in case it gets worse.", "D1 Afternoon Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it - 5, $r to "photo")]


:: D1 Afternoon Iris 2 [bg-hall-posters day iris]
(if: $r is "rip")[You fold it into a tiny square. Iris watches you do it.

"You didn't have to," she says. Then, smaller: "Thanks."

She walks to class without her hood up.](else:)[She sees your phone come up. Her face does something complicated.

"Right," she says. "Everyone's got one."

She's gone before you can explain.]

[[Keep going->D1 Late]]


:: D1 Afternoon Naomi [bg-fountain day naomi]
Naomi is on the edge of the fountain with her headphones around her neck, eating crackers out of the box. She holds the box out without looking at you.

"If you're here to talk about the poster thing, don't," she says. "Everyone's being so weird today."

(link-reveal-goto: "Take a cracker. Talk about literally anything else.", "D1 Afternoon Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it + 5, $r to "else")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"You're being kind of weird too.\"", "D1 Afternoon Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it - 5, $r to "weird")]


:: D1 Afternoon Naomi 2 [bg-fountain day naomi]
(if: $r is "else")[You argue for twenty minutes about whether the fountain guy is getting better at guitar. (He isn't.) She laughs once, then looks annoyed that she did.

"Okay, go," she says. "Some of us have class."](else:)["Wow." She closes the cracker box. "I'm the normal amount of weird. Thanks."

She puts her headphones back on. No music. You can tell.]

[[Keep going->D1 Late]]


:: D1 Late [bg-hall-brick day hub]
Late afternoon. The light goes orange on the brick. A group chat you're in has thirty new messages. You don't open it. You know what they're about.

(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devI >= $devN, "Go see if Iris made it back okay.", "You haven't checked on Iris in a while."), "D1 Late Iris")[(display: "pick iris")]
(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devN >= $devI, "Naomi's doing a grocery run. Go be useful.", "Naomi's carrying groceries alone. She'd never ask."), "D1 Late Naomi")[(display: "pick naomi")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Mute the chat. Go for a walk on your own.", "Alone")[(set: $next to "D1 Evening")(display: "go alone")]


:: D1 Late Iris [bg-room-iris day iris]
Iris is in the laundry room in her building, sitting on top of a dryer because it's warm and nobody comes down here. Her roommate has friends over. She could hear them through the wall.

"They weren't even being mean," she says. "They were just... talking about it. Like it's a show."

(link-reveal-goto: "Sit on the next dryer. Wait for her laundry with her.", "D1 Late Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it + 5, $r to "stay")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"Want me to go tell them to shut up?\"", "D1 Late Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it - 5, $r to "tell")]


:: D1 Late Iris 2 [bg-room-iris day iris]
(if: $r is "stay")[The dryer buzzes. She folds everything very carefully, even the socks.

When she's done she says, "This was nice. Is that weird? That this was nice?"

"No."](else:)["No," she says, too fast. "Please don't. It'll just be one more thing they talk about."

She pulls her knees up and waits for you to leave. You do.]

[[Keep going->D1 Evening]]


:: D1 Late Naomi [bg-cafe day naomi]
Naomi has three bags and a fake smile for the cashier. When she sees you, she hands you the heaviest bag immediately.

"I didn't ask you to come," she says.

"You didn't."

"So don't act like I owe you."

(link-reveal-goto: "Carry the bags. Let her complain the whole way.", "D1 Late Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it + 5, $r to "carry")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"You could just say thanks.\"", "D1 Late Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it - 5, $r to "thanks")]


:: D1 Late Naomi 2 [bg-cafe day naomi]
(if: $r is "carry")[She complains about the cashier, the bags, the weather, your shoes. At her door she takes the bags back.

"You have weird arms," she says. "Like, good for carrying. That's all I'm saying."

From Naomi, that's a parade.](else:)["Thanks," she says, flat, like you made her pay for it.

She doesn't let you carry anything else.]

[[Keep going->D1 Evening]]


:: D2 Afternoon [bg-library day hub]
Afternoon. You're supposed to be studying. Two tables over, someone is reading the post about Iris out loud, doing voices.

(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devI >= $devN, "Iris said she might come to the library. Meet her at the door.", "Iris might walk in on this. Head her off."), "D2 Afternoon Iris")[(display: "pick iris")]
(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devN >= $devI, "Naomi's somewhere in the stacks. Go find her.", "Naomi's in the stacks. You did kind of blow her off."), "D2 Afternoon Naomi")[(display: "pick naomi")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Put your hood up and leave. You can't listen to this.", "Alone")[(set: $next to "D2 Late")(display: "go alone")]


:: D2 Afternoon Iris [bg-library day iris]
You catch Iris at the library doors. She has her sketchbook under her arm and the face of someone who's been practising walking in.

"I just need one book," she says. "One. For class."

(link-reveal-goto: "\"Tell me which one. I'll get it. Wait out here.\"", "D2 Afternoon Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it + 5, $r to "get")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"Just go in. If you act normal, they'll stop.\"", "D2 Afternoon Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it - 5, $r to "normal")]


:: D2 Afternoon Iris 2 [bg-library day iris]
(if: $r is "get")[It takes you four minutes. When you come out, she's standing exactly where you left her, like she was scared to move.

She takes the book with both hands. "I owe you," she says.

"You don't."

"I do. Let me owe you."](else:)[She goes in. You watch her slow down at the table with the voices.

She turns around and walks straight back out, past you, without the book.]

[[Keep going->D2 Late]]


:: D2 Afternoon Naomi [bg-library day naomi]
Naomi is sitting on the floor between two shelves, which is not a Naomi thing to do. She's reading the same page of a textbook. When she sees you, she sits up straight, like you caught her at something.

"I'm studying," she says. "Obviously."

(link-reveal-goto: "Sit on the floor with her. Read the same page.", "D2 Afternoon Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it + 5, $r to "floor")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"Since when do you sit on the floor?\"", "D2 Afternoon Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it - 5, $r to "since")]


:: D2 Afternoon Naomi 2 [bg-library day naomi]
(if: $r is "floor")[You read the same page together about four times. Eventually she snorts.

"This book is so bad," she says, and her shoulders come down a little.](else:)["Since now," she says. "Is that allowed?"

She collects her things and goes to sit somewhere you can't see her.]

[[Keep going->D2 Late]]


:: D2 Late [bg-hall-brick day hub]
Late afternoon. The dining hall is about to close. Someone in the group chat has changed Iris's name to something you won't repeat.

(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devI >= $devN, "Pick up dinner for two. Take it to Iris.", "Iris probably hasn't eaten. Bring her something."), "D2 Late Iris")[(display: "pick iris")]
(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devN >= $devI, "Naomi sent a photo of a sad microwave meal. Fix that.", "Naomi sent a photo of a microwave meal. Just the photo."), "D2 Late Naomi")[(display: "pick naomi")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Leave the group chat. Eat by yourself.", "Alone")[(set: $next to "D2 Evening")(display: "go alone")]


:: D2 Late Iris [bg-room-iris day iris]
Iris eats on the floor with her back against her bed. Between bites she keeps checking her phone. Not the chat. Something else. Every time, she puts it back face down.

"Can I tell you something?" she says. Then: "Never mind. It's dumb."

(set: $mtFrom to "naomi")(display: "midtext")
|ch)[(link-reveal-goto: "\"Tell me when you want. I'm not going anywhere.\"", "D2 Late Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it + 5, $r to "wait")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"It's not dumb. Just tell me.\"", "D2 Late Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it - 5, $r to "push")]](if: $mtSkip)[(show: ?ch)]


:: D2 Late Iris 2 [bg-room-iris day iris]
(if: $r is "wait")[She nods. She doesn't tell you.

But she eats everything, and when you get up to leave she says, "Tonight. Maybe tonight."](else:)["It's dumb," she says again, firmer. She closes the container.

"I'm kind of tired." You know what that means.]

[[Keep going->D2 Evening]]


:: D2 Late Naomi [bg-room-naomi day naomi]
The microwave meal is still on her desk, half eaten. Naomi is on her bed, scrolling. She tilts the phone away when you come in. Too fast.

"I'm just reading stuff," she says. "People are so stupid. Like, who even //started// this?" She says it like a joke. She doesn't laugh.

(set: $mtFrom to "iris")(display: "midtext")
|ch)[(link-reveal-goto: "\"Who cares who started it. Put it down. Eat with me.\"", "D2 Late Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it + 5, $r to "eat")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"Does it matter who started it?\"", "D2 Late Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it - 5, $r to "matter")]](if: $mtSkip)[(show: ?ch)]


:: D2 Late Naomi 2 [bg-room-naomi day naomi]
(if: $r is "eat")[She puts the phone down. She eats your fries instead of her meal and calls them mid.

Halfway through, she goes quiet. "You'd tell me, right? If I did something bad?"

Before you can answer: "Forget it. Pass the ketchup."](else:)["No," she says. "Obviously not."

She keeps scrolling. You watch her read the same post three times.]

[[Keep going->D2 Evening]]


:: D3 Afternoon [bg-classroom day hub]
Afternoon. Your seminar. The professor is talking about ethics, which feels like a joke someone is playing on you specifically. Hale's office is on this floor. The door has a new sign on it: //on leave//.

(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devI >= $devN, "Iris has this seminar too. Sit next to her.", "Iris has this seminar. There's an empty seat by her. There always is now."), "D3 Afternoon Iris")[(display: "pick iris")]
(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devN >= $devI, "Naomi's waiting outside. She keeps texting the word 'bored'.", "Naomi's outside. She's texted 'bored' seven times."), "D3 Afternoon Naomi")[(display: "pick naomi")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Skip it. Go sit somewhere nobody knows you.", "Alone")[(set: $next to "D3 Late")(display: "go alone")]


:: D3 Afternoon Iris [bg-classroom day iris]
There's a space around Iris's desk, like a moat. You sit in it. A few people look. She stares at her notebook.

Halfway through, the professor asks the room whether a person is responsible for what happens to information after they pass it on. Someone in the back laughs. Iris's pen stops.

(link-reveal-goto: "Pass her a note: //want to leave? (I do)//", "D3 Afternoon Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it + 5, $r to "leave")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Answer the question out loud. Somebody should.", "D3 Afternoon Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it - 5, $r to "answer")]


:: D3 Afternoon Iris 2 [bg-classroom day iris]
(if: $r is "leave")[She reads it. She writes //yes// under it, very small.

You both walk out in the middle of the lecture and nobody stops you. Outside, she breathes like she's come up from underwater.

"That was so rude," she says. "Thank you."](else:)[You say something about responsibility. It's a good answer. It doesn't matter.

Everyone turns to look at Iris while you say it, because of course they do. She stares at her notebook until the end, and leaves first.]

[[Keep going->D3 Late]]


:: D3 Afternoon Naomi [bg-hall-posters day naomi]
Naomi is leaning on the wall outside your seminar with two drinks. Neither of them is coffee, which is a red flag.

"I couldn't do coffee today," she says. "My stomach's being stupid."

She pushes a lemonade at you.

(link-reveal-goto: "\"Walk with me. Anywhere. Your choice.\"", "D3 Afternoon Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it + 5, $r to "walk")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"Your stomach? Are you okay?\"", "D3 Afternoon Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it - 5, $r to "okay")]


:: D3 Afternoon Naomi 2 [bg-hall-posters day naomi]
(if: $r is "walk")[She picks the long way round the lake, which is the most sentimental thing you've ever seen her do. She doesn't talk much.

Once, at the water, she says, "Do you ever feel like you did something bad and you just don't know what yet?"

Then: "Ignore me. Low blood sugar."](else:)[She curls her hands into fists around the cup.

"I'm fine. God. It's just a stomach."

She drinks her lemonade very fast and says she has to go.]

[[Keep going->D3 Late]]


:: D3 Late [bg-hall-brick day hub]
Early evening. The sky over the quad goes pink and nobody looks at it.

(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devI >= $devN, "Go find Iris before dinner.", "Go find Iris. You owe her more than a text."), "D3 Late Iris")[(display: "pick iris")]
(link-reveal-goto: (cond: $devN >= $devI, "Catch Naomi before dinner.", "Check on Naomi. She's been off all day."), "D3 Late Naomi")[(display: "pick naomi")]
(link-reveal-goto: "Kill an hour on your own first.", "Alone")[(set: $next to "D3 Evening")(display: "go alone")]


:: D3 Late Iris [bg-gallery day iris]
You meet Iris in the art hallway near her building. She's taped one of her drawings to the wall between two real ones, as a joke. Nobody has noticed.

"It's been up for three days," she says. "Nobody looks at anything." She sounds almost happy about it.

(set: $mtFrom to "naomi")(display: "midtext")
|ch)[(link-reveal-goto: "\"I'm looking at it.\" Actually look at it.", "D3 Late Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it + 5, $r to "look")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"Should you be doing stuff like that? With everything?\"", "D3 Late Iris 2")[(set: $iris to it - 5, $r to "should")]](if: $mtSkip)[(show: ?ch)]


:: D3 Late Iris 2 [bg-gallery day iris]
(if: $r is "look")[It's her window, at night, in blue. You look at it for a long time.

When you turn around, she's watching you instead of the drawing. "Okay," she says. "Okay." She leaves the drawing up.](else:)[She takes it down. Folds it in half.

"Right," she says. "Probably not."]

[[Keep going->D3 Evening]]


:: D3 Late Naomi [bg-library day naomi]
Naomi is on the bench outside the library with her laptop, writing an email to her mom. She deletes //I'm fine// and types it again.

"My mom thinks I sound weird on the phone," she says. "I don't sound weird."

Her voice cracks on //weird//, which is unlucky for her.

(set: $mtFrom to "iris")(display: "midtext")
|ch)[(link-reveal-goto: "\"Call her. I'll sit here while you do.\"", "D3 Late Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it + 5, $r to "call")]
(link-reveal-goto: "\"You kind of do sound weird.\"", "D3 Late Naomi 2")[(set: $naomi to it - 5, $r to "weird")]](if: $mtSkip)[(show: ?ch)]


:: D3 Late Naomi 2 [bg-library day naomi]
(if: $r is "call")[She calls. She talks about her classes in a bright fake voice for six minutes. Near the end, quietly, she says, "No, I'm okay. I have a friend here."

She hangs up and doesn't look at you. "Don't," she says. You don't.](else:)["Great. Super." She shuts the laptop on the email. "Everyone's a critic."

She doesn't send it.]

[[Keep going->D3 Evening]]


:: D3 Night [bg-vending night maeve]
(if: $loop is 2)[Maeve is waiting at the vending machine, exactly like last time. Your chips are already in the tray. Gummy worms too.

"Hi, babe," she says. "Our date night."

She steps close. Closer than last time. Her coat smells like cold air and something sweet, like flowers left too long in a vase. "Last time you said yes. I've thought about it all week. Well. All //two// weeks."

She tilts her head. "Say yes again. I dare you."

You're nearly sure what she is now. Seventy-five percent. Maybe more. The motion light above her hasn't come on once.

(link-goto: "Go with her. You know what it means.", "End Forever")
[[Not this time.->D3 Walk]]](else:)[On the way out of Iris's building, you stop at a vending machine for something to do with your hands.

(if: $metMaeve)[Maeve is leaning on it. Of course she is.](else:)[There's a girl leaning on it. Long white hair. Pale eyes. "I'm Maeve," she says, like you asked.](set: $metMaeve to true)

"So," she says. "Our date. I said I'd make you forget everything for a few hours. I keep my promises, babe."

You don't remember agreeing to a date. You don't remember not agreeing, either.

[[Go with her.->D3 Date]]
[[Not tonight.->D3 Walk]]]


:: D3 Date [bg-gallery night maeve]
(if: $alone >= 6)[(go-to: "D3 Date Die")](else:)[(set: $dating to true)She takes you somewhere you've never noticed on campus, a long hallway full of art, lit teal and orange. It's empty. It's always empty, she says, at this hour.

She talks about nothing. She laughs at everything you say. For three hours you don't think about the rain once.

When she hugs you goodnight it's perfect. Warm. Her hands are like ice.

"Same time tomorrow, babe," she says. It isn't a question.

Your phone has two missed texts. You don't open them until morning.

(link-reveal-goto: "Go to bed.", "End of day")[(set: $walked to "maeve")]]


:: D3 Date Die [bg-gallery night maeve]
She takes you to a long hallway full of art, lit teal and orange. It's empty. It's always empty, she says, at this hour.

She talks about nothing. She laughs at everything you say. You don't think about the rain once. You don't think about Iris once. You haven't really thought about either of them all week.

Somewhere around midnight she rests her head on your shoulder.

"You know," she says, "you're the first one in ages who came to me on purpose."

Her hands are so cold. Your hands are getting cold too.

You look at your phone. 2:07.

"Oh, babe," Maeve says, very softly. Almost fond. "Already?"

[[...->Again]]


:: End Forever [bg-gallery night maeve]
She takes you to the art hallway again. Teal and orange. Empty.

This time you know. Ninety percent. Ninety-nine. You go anyway.

"Look at you," Maeve says, delighted, pulling you down onto the bench by both hands. "Second time. On purpose. Do you know how rare you are?"

"Are you going to tell me what you are?"

"You already know, babe." She kisses you. It's like snow, and then it isn't like anything.

Somewhere very far away, two phones light up with your name, and nobody is there to answer them.

Somewhere very close, Maeve laughs, warm, right against your ear. "Mine, then," she says. "For good this time."

It doesn't end. It just stops being a week.

[[...->Credits]]


:: D4 Afternoon [bg-stairwell day hub]
